From f411748ffcdb6195f5b057a0f4df0adc03396e53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 13:46:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 002/638] base: define the pre-MMU AROS allocation substrate
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-base-runtime

AI_STATUS: wip

ROOT_CAUSE: PartitionAlloc assumes reservable virtual address space, page-state transitions, process-local TLS, and platform stack diagnostics; AROS currently exposes Exec allocation but not the complete mmap/mprotect reservation contract.

FIX_REASON: Add an explicit AROS allocator backend and platform adapters that preserve allocation ownership and compilation while exposing the current protection limitations. This is a bring-up substrate, not a claim that W^X or sparse reservations already work.

SCOPE: base/allocator dispatcher TLS, PartitionAlloc page allocation, entropy, thread identity, stack trace, and StarScan compatibility.

VALIDATION: the native Chromium base probe passed under SMP QEMU and the headless graph compiled through PartitionAlloc consumers into Mojo and Skia.

RISK: high until OPAL/MMU page mapping and protection transitions replace the allocation-backed reservation model.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
